{# LXD product template — reproduces the structure of LXD's published release
   notes in canonical/lxd: doc/reference/release-notes/<track>/release-notes-<ver>.md
   (reference documents: release-notes-6.10.1.md and release-notes-6.10.0.md).

   How it differs from base.md.j2 and why:
   - LXD notes have NO date line, NO DA186 intro-links line, and NO
     Compatibility section — LXD is a snap, not a charm; compatibility facts
     (minimum Go version, snap channel) live in dedicated sections instead.
     The base template's hard-coded "## Compatibility" heading is suppressed
     by overriding the `compatibility_heading` block to be empty.
   - Section order mirrors the LXD release-notes-template.md convention:
     frontmatter, anchor, title, LTS/feature sentence, admonition, Highlights,
     UI updates, Bug fixes, Backwards-incompatible changes, Known issues,
     Updated minimum Go version, Snap packaging changes, Change log,
     Downloads.
   - Entries use LXD's bullet style: "- [{spellexception}`message`](PR URL)"
     (single links, no commit links, no Jira prefix).
   - The changelog block maps the builder's fixed DA186 categories onto LXD's
     own sections: Features → Highlights (agent restructures manually into
     per-feature ### sections), Bug fixes stay, everything else ("Other
     improvements", "Breaking changes", "Security") is reorganised by the
     agent into the LXD sections; the template renders the raw categories and
     the polish pass reshapes them.
   - Sections the builder cannot populate (UI updates, Known issues, Go
     version, Snap packaging) are emitted as clearly marked TODO comments for
     the agent's polish pass.

   Reference release notes live at:
   https://github.com/canonical/lxd/blob/main/doc/reference/release-notes/6/
#}
